From ff2d2c367c4007430519afc6484bfb8f71370d19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeongyeon Kim <jeongyeon@Jeongyeonui-MacBookAir.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 14:57:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Let obstacle_size be set from a params file

Setting obstacle_size in a params file killed the bridge at startup:

    rclpy.exceptions.ParameterAlreadyDeclaredException:
        ('Parameter(s) already declared', ['obstacle_size'])

This node is constructed with
automatically_declare_parameters_from_overrides=True, so a parameter that
appears in a params file, on the command line or in a launch file is
already declared by the time __init__ runs, and declare_parameter() on it
raises. agent_collisions below already carries a has_parameter guard for
exactly this; obstacle_size did not.

Needed because the bridge's own default of 2 (a cell radius, so 0.20 m
square) is too small for the stack to react to: detect drops any scan
cluster under min_obs_size = 10 laser points, and at gym's 4.7 rad / 1080
beams an 0.20 m obstacle only spans 10 points inside 4.6 m. Measured 8
points at 5.5 m with /perception/obstacles staying empty, so no evasion
was ever planned. config/SIM/sim.yaml now asks for obstacle_size: 4
(0.40 m), which needs this guard to launch at all.

Behaviour is unchanged when the parameter is not overridden: the guard
falls through to the same declare_parameter() and the same default of 2.
---
 f1tenth_gym_ros/gym_bridge.py | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/f1tenth_gym_ros/gym_bridge.py b/f1tenth_gym_ros/gym_bridge.py
index 6743bdd..e2c718a 100644
--- a/f1tenth_gym_ros/gym_bridge.py
+++ b/f1tenth_gym_ros/gym_bridge.py
@@ -114,9 +114,15 @@ class GymBridge(Node):
         self.set_descriptor(name='kb_teleop', descriptor=ParameterDescriptor(
             type=ParameterType.PARAMETER_BOOL, description="Whether teleop is enabled"))
 
-        self.declare_parameter('obstacle_size', 2, descriptor=ParameterDescriptor(
-            type=ParameterType.PARAMETER_INTEGER,
-            description="Cell radius painted into /map per /clicked_point obstacle"))
+        # has_parameter guard for the same reason as agent_collisions below: this node
+        # is constructed with automatically_declare_parameters_from_overrides=True, so
+        # setting obstacle_size in a params file (config/SIM/sim.yaml does) already
+        # declares it, and an unguarded declare_parameter() raises
+        # ParameterAlreadyDeclaredException and kills the bridge at startup.
+        if not self.has_parameter('obstacle_size'):
+            self.declare_parameter('obstacle_size', 2, descriptor=ParameterDescriptor(
+                type=ParameterType.PARAMETER_INTEGER,
+                description="Cell radius painted into /map per /clicked_point obstacle"))
         self.obstacle_size = self.get_parameter('obstacle_size').value
 
         # Off by default, which is upstream f1tenth_gym behaviour: the iTTC check runs
